      "claim": "Outdoor temperature in November is an external environmental variable that directly affects heating and cooling loads, thereby influencing electricity consumption, and it cannot be controlled by the students.",
      "evidence": "Energy‑consumption models show a strong correlation between temperature and electricity use; weather varies unpredictably.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": [1, 2]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "claim": "Because temperature is both uncontrollable and variable, it is the most uncontrollable factor among the options.",
      "evidence": "Steps 3‑6 evaluate each option; only temperature meets both criteria of being beyond student control and having a direct, variable impact on the bill.",
